# R4 SEV-1 regression: solo-tab drag past strip-edge orphaned the pane.
# Repro: single pane in the layout, drag its tab from inside the chip past
# the strip's right edge into whitespace. Expected: no-op (pane stays
# visible in the strip); actual (pre-fix): chip vanished, editor showed
# welcome/logo, pane still in App::panes but no clickable rect.
# See: findings/mnml-hunt-2026-08-06-vscode-mouse-r4/sev1.md
write b.txt BBBBBBBB
command view.toggle_tree
open b.txt

# One pane, one tab. b.txt visible.
expect screen contains "BBBBBBBB"
expect pane "b.txt"

# Drag from inside the chip (col 5, row 1) past strip whitespace to col 100.
drag 5 1 100 1

# Post-drop: nothing should have changed — b.txt still the only pane,
# still visible, and its tab chip is still on the strip. The R3 dest_survivor
# guard in `drop_tab_on_strip` (src/app/tab_drop.rs:153) covers this:
# when the src tab is the leaf's only tab (dest_survivor.is_none()),
# bail before touching the layout so src stays visible.
expect screen contains "BBBBBBBB"
expect pane "b.txt"
# The tab chip is still on the strip — 󰈙 is the file glyph rendered
# before the b.txt label in the per-leaf strip.
expect screen contains "b.txt"
